            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Views on Music and Society</strong><br>\nRubinstein believed in music as a universal language and advocated for its ability to transcend cultural and national barriers, a view that was reflected in his eclectic style.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Later Years and Autobiography</strong><br>\nIn his later years, Rubinstein focused more on composing and writing, including his autobiography, which provides insights into his life and the musical culture of his time.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Death and Posthumous Recognition</strong><br>\nAnton Rubinstein died on November 20, 1894. While his playing style is lost to time, his contributions to music education and his role in the development of Russian classical music remain significant.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
